From f43b0e5f7ae07a6349860637af6ddcadb0c1b724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WizardsAcademy <357366786+WizardsAcademy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:56:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Noa's broken animations: real walk cycle, no squash-shear
 hurt, no rotated die

Root causes found by measuring the shipped sheet:
- 'attack' was f13(lunge) -> f11(attack) -> f2(A WALKING FRAME). Now idle -> attack -> splash.
- 'walk_down' sliced the idle in half and lifted each half 2px, opening a seam
  across her body. Now it uses the two real front-facing idle poses.
- 'hurt' rescaled a walk frame vertically by 0.9 and sheared it 3px -> grey smear.
  Now it uses the drawn recoil pose, shunted 1px with a re-inked impact edge.
- 'die' rotated the idle by -76 deg then rescaled to 56x25 -> unreadable smear.
  Now it sinks the authored body behind a rising crimson dissolve line.
- 'walk' used 4 unrelated art_src files as if they were cycle phases.
  Now it is one genuine pose + lower-body mirror + contact/bob frames.

Also fixed a 1px transparent seam my own mirror helper introduced (row 59-60).

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
